  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Feel Like a Stranger** (1 review): Reviewer found the opener disjointed, so it failed to give the strong start they expect from it [5]\n- **Cumberland Blues** (1 review): Reviewer says it nearly collapsed, confirming a rough start to the summer tour [5]\n- **It Must Have Been the Roses** (1 review): Reviewer says this was the first time the band played the song [6]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **It Must Have Been the Roses**: rare: 7 archived performances [7]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **deadco2019-06-07.Nak300.CP4.flac24** (recommended): source not stated; 18 songs; 175 min; rated 4.4/5 by 5 [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- The sunset was the most amazing the reviewer had ever seen [6]\n- It got very cold; a Texas attendee was unprepared for the chill [6]\n- Second set improved and was enjoyable, though it didn't reach the heights the band sometimes hits [5]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **deadco2019-06-07.Nak300.CP4.flac24**: taped by John Hermsen; transferred by John Hermsen; source: Nakamich cm300 w/ CP4 Shotguns (Sank P48 Mod) > Sound Devices 722 [1]. Also: Recorded with Nakamichi CM300 mics and CP4 shotgun capsules, into a Sound Devices 722 at 24-bit/48kHz [1]\n\n## Art and photos\n\n- Fan art by Psychedelic Cheerleader: [Dead and Company at The Gorge Amphitheater 2019 — TrippingDelightFantastic](https://www.trippingdelightfantastic.com/home/dead-and-company-at-the-gorge-amphitheater-2019) [8]\n- Fan art by Psychedelic Cheerleader: [Dead and Company at The Gorge Amphitheater 2019 — TrippingDelightFantastic](https://www.trippingdelightfantastic.com/home/dead-and-company-at-the-gorge-amphitheater-2019) [9]",
